# # /vaimee/
#
# Permanent identifiers for vocabularies published by VAIMEE S.r.l.
#
# https://w3id.org/vaimee/awm          AgoràWasteMap, the by-product vocabulary
# https://w3id.org/vaimee/awm/sources  its data source inventory module
# https://w3id.org/vaimee/awm/legal    its regulatory framework module
# https://w3id.org/vaimee/awm/shapes   the SHACL constraints the data is validated against
#
# Terms are minted in one namespace, https://w3id.org/vaimee/awm#, and the
# document served there is the union of the three modules, so any term resolves
# to a document that defines it. 303 because the identifier names a concept and
# the redirect leads to a document about it.
#
# ## Contact
# This space is administered by:
#
# Luca Roffia
# GitHub username: lroffia
#
# VAIMEE S.r.l. — https://vaimee.com

RewriteEngine on

# The three ontology documents. Exact matches, and they come first: the legal
# module is /awm/legal, while the acts it cites are /awm/legal/<act>, and a
# loose rule here would swallow them.
RewriteRule ^awm$          https://wastemap.vaimee.com/ontology/awm [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^awm/sources$  https://wastemap.vaimee.com/ontology/awm-sources [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^awm/legal$    https://wastemap.vaimee.com/ontology/awm-legal [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^awm/shapes$   https://wastemap.vaimee.com/ontology/awm-shapes [R=303,L]

# Individuals named by the vocabulary — categories, sources, legal acts,
# territorial estimates. They are described in the knowledge graph rather than
# served one document each, so for now they land on the ontology index, which
# explains the model and links to the public query console. This rule is
# expected to become per-resource once the graph is published for dereferencing.
RewriteRule ^awm/          https://wastemap.vaimee.com/ontology/ [R=302,L]

# Anything else under this identifier.
RewriteRule ^(.*)$         https://vaimee.com/$1 [R=302,L]
